# Screen text (pen). Keys are "pen-" plus a short name from the English text; tooltip keys end in -tip.

pen-not-enough-strokes = Not enough strokes
pen-the-pressure-barely-varies = The pressure barely varies
pen-low = Low
pen-pen-pressure-at-or-below = Pen pressure at or below this counts as zero (ignores the light touches)
pen-high = High
pen-pen-pressure-at-or-above = Pen pressure at or above this counts as full (reach the maximum without pressing hard)
pen-draw-a-few-strokes-at-tip = Draw a few strokes at your usual strength. The strokes are not part of the project
pen-auto = Auto
pen-low-high-and-curve-from = Low, high and curve from the drawn strokes
pen-clear = Clear
pen-removes-the-drawn-strokes = Removes the drawn strokes
pen-revert = Revert
pen-goes-back-to-the-adjustment = Goes back to the adjustment from when Pen was opened
pen-default = Default
pen-back-to-low-0-high = Back to low 0%, high 100% and a straight line
pen-using-windows-ink-because-no = Using Windows Ink because no WinTab driver was found.
pen-using-windows-ink-because-the = Using Windows Ink because the WinTab driver did not respond.
pen-using-windows-ink-because-no-2 = Using Windows Ink because no WinTab tablet was found.
pen-using-windows-ink-because-wintab = Using Windows Ink because WinTab could not be opened.
